    "notes": "The named PMTiles precinct, the Khuê Văn pavilion and the Thiên Quang Well fix the location and signed axis. The five courts, five main passages, five pools and circular pavilion window remain open across all four detail levels. The five-court exterior follows the PMTiles buildings, pools and paths. Eave profiles, wall heights and individual stele bases are photo-based reconstructions. The pavilions and approach thresholds fit the standard elevation samples. Water, planting and roads use host data. Roof ornament and inscription relief are represented at viewing scale. Interior shrines and legible inscriptions are outside this exterior model."
